{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>and he was not</b> Since they came to say \"he died in his sin,\" they needed to say: he was not among the complainers and not among the assembly of Korah who banded together against HaShem, but rather in his sin alone, and he did not cause others to sin with him — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Numbers 27:3). And he did not explain why they would come to say \"he died in his sin,\" but rather they would say \"our father died in the wilderness and he had no sons,\" for that is indeed what was fitting to say. But according to the opinion of our Sages (Bava Batra 118a), they needed to say that he was not in the assembly of Korah, because the assembly of Korah had no portion in the land, and likewise the complainers who were in the assembly of Korah, for this was heard among the people from the court of Moses. And thus Ibn Ezra explained and said: the daughters thought that those who gathered against YHWH would not inherit. And my opinion, by way of the plain sense, is that they said this because they thought that Moses our teacher hated the assembly of Korah more than all the other sinners who died in the wilderness, for they were the ones who rose up against him and denied all his deeds, and they thought that perhaps in his hatred of them he would say: \"Let there be none to extend kindness to him, nor any to favor his fatherless children; may the iniquity of his fathers be remembered before YHWH\" (Psalms 109:12, 14). Therefore they informed him that he was not among them. And they further hinted that he was not among those who died in the plagues, but he died in the wilderness upon his bed. And the reason for <b>for he died in his sin</b> — they said: he died in the wilderness in his sin, in that he did not merit to enter the land; or according to the words of Rabbi Judah ha-Levi the poet, of blessed memory, who explained that it is connected with \"and he had no sons,\" as one would say today, \"because of sins such-and-such happened.\""], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:15.646776548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}